      "message": "No, only that everything that starts with \"a/\" is in a contiguous subslice.  The relationship between \"a/\" and \"a.\" is undefined by this requirement, as is the relationship between \"b/\" and \"a.\".  It is implemented by a normal byte-by-byte sort except that \"/\" comes before everything else (including \".\").",
